{title: Over Jordan}
{subtitle: Joshua 3:14–17; Deuteronomy 34:1–4}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
On Nebo's height old Moses stood
And looked on Canaan's land
The Lord showed him the promised good
Laid out on every hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bbmaj7]The priests went down [C]to Jordan's [Dm]flood
[Bb]The ark [C]upon their [F]shoulders [Am]high
[Bb]The waters stood [C]up where they [Dm]stood
[Bb]And Israel [C]passed by [Dm]dry
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
So when I come [C]to Jordan's [Bb]side
And [C]hear the waters [Dm]roar
The Lord will part [C]the swelling [Bb]tide
And [Gm7]lead me safe[Am7]ly o[Dm]'er
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Then [Bb]I shall stand on [C]Canaan's [Dm]ground
And [Bb]see the [C]promised [F][Am]land
Where [Bb]milk and honey flow [C]a[Dm]round
[Bb]At God's own [C]right hand
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro}
